{
  "kanji": "落",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 落\ntitle: fall down\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-3, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 12\nradical: 艸\nradicalNumber: 140\nonyomi: [ラク]\nkunyomi: [お.ちる, お.ち, お.とす]\ndistractors: [葉, 薬, 茶]\n---\n\n# 落 — fall down\n\n**Strokes:** 12 · **Key (radical):** 艸 (no. 140) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n落 connects a downward movement with something losing its position. In [落ちる](../words/落ちる.md) おちる,\nthe thing itself falls; 落とす おとす describes someone dropping it.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** under the plant top 艹, imagine the water-shaped left part\ncarrying something downward past the 各 shape. This is a memory aid, not a historical derivation.\nThe indexing radical 艸 appears here as 艹.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| お.ちる | kun | [落ちる](../words/落ちる.md) おちる — fall |\n| お.とす | kun | 落とす おとす — drop something |\n| ラク | on | 落下 らっか — a fall; descent |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [落ちる](../words/落ちる.md) おちる — fall down\n- 落とす おとす — drop; let fall\n- 落下 らっか — falling; descent\n\n## Notes\n\n葉が落ちる (はがおちる) means \"a leaf falls.\" 葉を落とす (はをおとす) instead presents\nthe leaf as the object being dropped or shed.\n[葉](葉.md), [薬](薬.md), and [茶](茶.md) share the plant top, but their lower shapes differ.\nDo not identify 落 from 艹 alone.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project).\n\nVocabulary: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1548550, 1589260, 1548650.\n",
